IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc32-nif-xxi1.l4 -- AMENDMENTS NOT IN FORCE: PART XXI.1 Miscarriage of Justice Reviews, as replaced by 2024, c. 33, s. 3, with ss 5 and 6 of that Act (sections 696.7 "applicant" and 696.72),
-- from the end of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (lines 19549-19649 of the text).
-- Part ccc32, layer 1. This is a SECOND, FUTURE text of Part XXI.1, which ccc24 encodes in its in-force form: every name here carries `(not in force)` after the section label so that it cannot collide with theirs.
-- NOTHING in this module says the text is law today. The accused is the APPLICANT of this Part: it gives the person who has been found guilty (or found a dangerous offender, or not criminally responsible)
-- a review by a Commission, outside the appeal courts, and (section 679(7), in ccc32-nif-1.l4) release or detention pending the review as though an appellant.
-- The Commission, the court of appeal and the relevant Attorney General are not in the core's Party type as parties of this Part: this module declares its own party type (NEEDS-CORE.md).
-- How a result reads, the naming rule and the rule for days the text leaves open: see the head of ccc32-related-1.l4 and NOTES.md. A duty with no period in the text is a regulative rule WITHOUT a WITHIN
-- ("as expeditiously as possible", "on a regular basis", "on receipt" fix no number), and each duty is also a decision function (a DEONTIC cannot be asserted on the stable binary).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30). It is not the official text,
-- and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.

§ `2024, c. 33, s. 3 -- Part XXI.1 replaced; section 696.1 definitions`

-- 3 Part XXI.1 of the Act is replaced by the following: [Part XXI.1 Miscarriage of Justice Reviews] 696.1 The following definitions apply in this Part.
-- applicant, in relation to a miscarriage of justice review application, means the person who is the subject of the finding or verdict in question.
-- Commission means the Miscarriage of Justice Review Commission established under subsection 696.71(1).
-- court of appeal means the court of appeal for the province in which the matter that is the subject of the application was heard.
-- src:19550 | 3 Part XXI.1 of the Act is replaced by the following:
