§ `Review -- sections 696.3 to 696.6`

-- 696.3 (1) The Commission must deal with an application as expeditiously as possible and provide the applicant with an update concerning the status of their application on a regular basis.
-- No period is stated ("as expeditiously as possible", "on a regular basis"): no WITHIN. The decision twin says when the duty is owed.
-- src:19570 | Review
-- src:19571 | Handling of application
-- src:19572 | 696.3 (1) The Commission must deal with an application as expeditiously as possible and provide the applicant with an update concerning the status of their application on a regular basis.
@ref s 696.3(1) (not in force) (src:19570-19572)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 696.1 (not in force) party` `s 696.1 (not in force) act`
`s 696.3(1) (not in force) the Commission must deal with the application as expeditiously as possible` MEANS
    PARTY `s 696.1 (not in force) the Commission`
    MUST `s 696.3(1) (not in force) deal with the application as expeditiously as possible`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 696.1 (not in force) the Commission` BECAUSE "the Commission did not deal with the application as expeditiously as possible"

