-- In making the decision, the Commission must take into account (a) the amount of time that has passed since the final judgment of the trial court; (b) the reasons why the finding or verdict was not appealed; (c) whether it would serve a useful purpose for an application to be made
-- for an extension of the period within which a notice of appeal or of application for leave to appeal may be served and filed; (d) whether the application is supported by a new matter of significance that (i) ... (ii) ... (iii) ...; and (e) any other factor that it considers relevant.
-- src:19585 | (a) the amount of time that has passed since the final judgment of the trial court;
-- src:19586 | (b) the reasons why the finding or verdict was not appealed to the court of appeal or the Supreme Court of Canada;
-- src:19587 | (c) whether it would serve a useful purpose for an application to be made for an extension of the period within which a notice of appeal or a notice of application for leave to appeal, as the case may be, to the court of appeal or the Supreme Court of Canada may be served and filed;
-- src:19588 | (d) whether the application is supported by a new matter of significance that
-- src:19589 | (i) was not considered by the courts or previously considered by the Commission in an application in relation to the same finding or verdict,
-- src:19590 | (ii) requires investigation, and
-- src:19591 | (iii) does not raise only a question of law; and
-- src:19592 | (e) any other factor that it considers relevant.
@ref s 696.4(4)(a) to (e) (not in force) (src:19585-19592)
DECLARE `s 696.4(4) (not in force) the factor` IS ONE OF
    `s 696.4(4)(a) (not in force) the amount of time that has passed since the final judgment of the trial court`
    `s 696.4(4)(b) (not in force) the reasons why the finding or verdict was not appealed to the court of appeal or the Supreme Court of Canada`
    `s 696.4(4)(c) (not in force) whether it would serve a useful purpose for an application to be made for an extension of the period within which a notice of appeal or a notice of application for leave to appeal, as the case may be, to the court of appeal or the Supreme Court of Canada may be served and filed`
    `s 696.4(4)(d) (not in force) whether the application is supported by a new matter of significance`
    `s 696.4(4)(e) (not in force) any other factor that it considers relevant`

@ref s 696.4(4)(a) to (e) (not in force) (src:19585-19592)
GIVEN factor IS A `s 696.4(4) (not in force) the factor`
      `the Commission considers the factor relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.4(4) (not in force) the Commission must take the factor into account` MEANS
    CONSIDER factor
    WHEN `s 696.4(4)(a) (not in force) the amount of time that has passed since the final judgment of the trial court` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 696.4(4)(b) (not in force) the reasons why the finding or verdict was not appealed to the court of appeal or the Supreme Court of Canada` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 696.4(4)(c) (not in force) whether it would serve a useful purpose for an application to be made for an extension of the period within which a notice of appeal or a notice of application for leave to appeal, as the case may be, to the court of appeal or the Supreme Court of Canada may be served and filed` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 696.4(4)(d) (not in force) whether the application is supported by a new matter of significance` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 696.4(4)(e) (not in force) any other factor that it considers relevant` THEN
        IF `the Commission considers the factor relevant`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any other factor that it considers relevant"

-- (4)(d)(i) to (iii): a new matter of significance that was not considered by the courts or previously by the Commission on the same finding or verdict, that requires investigation, and that does not raise only a question of law.
-- "significance" is the Commission's judgment (a plain input); the three limbs are conjunctive; where one fails the text neither says yes nor no (NOTHING, a marginal reading).
-- src:19588 | (d) whether the application is supported by a new matter of significance that
-- src:19589 | (i) was not considered by the courts or previously considered by the Commission in an application in relation to the same finding or verdict,
-- src:19590 | (ii) requires investigation, and
-- src:19591 | (iii) does not raise only a question of law; and
@ref s 696.4(4)(d)(i) to (iii) (not in force) (src:19588-19591)
GIVEN `the matter is a new matter of significance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was not considered by the courts or previously considered by the Commission in an application in relation to the same finding or verdict` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it requires investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it does not raise only a question of law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.4(4)(d) (not in force) the application is supported by a new matter of significance that meets subparagraphs (i) to (iii)` MEANS
    IF `the matter is a new matter of significance`
       AND `it was not considered by the courts or previously considered by the Commission in an application in relation to the same finding or verdict`
       AND `it requires investigation`
       AND `it does not raise only a question of law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "a new matter of significance" is not defined and subparagraphs (i) to (iii) describe the matter without saying what else it must be

