-- Named for a power (the Commission "may conduct an investigation"): when the "If" gate fails the grant is limited by its own wording, so NOTHING, not JUST FALSE (the other reading is fork F24 in NOTES.md).
`s 696.5(1) (not in force) the Commission may conduct an investigation in relation to the application` MEANS
    IF `the Commission has reasonable grounds to believe that a miscarriage of justice may have occurred` OR `the Commission considers that it is in the interests of justice to conduct an investigation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the Commission has reasonable grounds to believe that a miscarriage of justice may have occurred or considers that it is in the interests of justice to do so"

-- (2) The Commission must send a notice to the applicant and to the relevant Attorney General indicating whether an investigation will be conducted. If the notice indicates that no investigation will be conducted,
-- the notice must also specify a reasonable period within which the applicant and the Attorney General may provide further information to the Commission in relation to the application.
-- src:19597 | Notice
-- src:19598 | (2) The Commission must send a notice to the applicant and to the relevant Attorney General indicating whether an investigation will be conducted. If the notice indicates that no investigation will be conducted, the notice must also specify a reasonable period within which the applicant and the Attorney General may provide further information to the Commission in relation to the application.
@ref s 696.5(2) (not in force) (src:19597-19598)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 696.1 (not in force) party` `s 696.1 (not in force) act`
`s 696.5(2) (not in force) the Commission must send a notice indicating whether an investigation will be conducted` MEANS
    PARTY `s 696.1 (not in force) the Commission`
    MUST `s 696.5(2) (not in force) send a notice to the applicant and to the relevant Attorney General indicating whether an investigation will be conducted`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 696.1 (not in force) the Commission` BECAUSE "the Commission did not send a notice to the applicant and to the relevant Attorney General indicating whether an investigation will be conducted"

@ref s 696.5(2) (not in force) (src:19597-19598)
GIVEN `an application is before the Commission and the Commission is deciding whether to conduct an investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.5(2) (not in force) the Commission owes the duty to send a notice indicating whether an investigation will be conducted` MEANS
    IF `an application is before the Commission and the Commission is deciding whether to conduct an investigation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says the notice must indicate whether an investigation will be conducted and says nothing of when it falls due

@ref s 696.5(2) (not in force) (src:19597-19598)
GIVEN `the notice indicates that no investigation will be conducted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.5(2) (not in force) the notice must also specify a reasonable period within which further information may be provided` MEANS
    IF `the notice indicates that no investigation will be conducted`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the notice indicates that no investigation will be conducted, the notice must also specify a reasonable period"

-- (3) The Commission may make a decision under section 696.6 without having conducted an investigation only if the period specified in the notice has ended. "only if": a necessary condition, so JUST FALSE before the period ends; once it has ended the bar is lifted (JUST TRUE).
-- src:19599 | Decision after notice
-- src:19600 | (3) The Commission may make a decision under section 696.6 without having conducted an investigation only if the period specified in the notice has ended.
@ref s 696.5(3) (not in force) (src:19599-19600)
GIVEN `the period specified in the notice has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.5(3) (not in force) the condition for deciding under section 696.6 without an investigation is met` MEANS
    IF `the period specified in the notice has ended`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "without having conducted an investigation only if the period specified in the notice has ended"

-- (4) For the purposes of an investigation, the Commission has the powers of a commissioner under Part I of the Inquiries Act.
-- src:19601 | Powers
-- src:19602 | (4) For the purposes of an investigation, the Commission has the powers of a commissioner under Part I of the Inquiries Act.
@ref s 696.5(4) (not in force) (src:19601-19602)
GIVEN `the purpose is an investigation in relation to an application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.5(4) (not in force) the Commission has the powers of a commissioner under Part I of the Inquiries Act` MEANS
    IF `the purpose is an investigation in relation to an application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of an investigation"

-- (5) The Commission may, on the terms it considers appropriate, authorize any of its employees, or a person under contract to it who has technical or specialized knowledge, to exercise the Commission's powers referred to in subsection (4).
-- src:19603 | Authorization
-- src:19604 | (5) The Commission may, on the terms it considers appropriate, authorize any of its employees, or a person under contract to it who has technical or specialized knowledge, to exercise the Commission’s powers referred to in subsection (4).
@ref s 696.5(5) (not in force) (src:19603-19604)
DECLARE `s 696.5(5) (not in force) the person` IS ONE OF
    `s 696.5(5) (not in force) an employee of the Commission`
    `s 696.5(5) (not in force) a person under contract to the Commission who has technical or specialized knowledge`
    `s 696.5(5) (not in force) a person of another kind`

@ref s 696.5(5) (not in force) (src:19603-19604)
GIVEN person IS A `s 696.5(5) (not in force) the person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.5(5) (not in force) the Commission may authorize the person to exercise the powers referred to in subsection (4)` MEANS
    CONSIDER person
    WHEN `s 696.5(5) (not in force) an employee of the Commission` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 696.5(5) (not in force) a person under contract to the Commission who has technical or specialized knowledge` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 696.5(5) (not in force) a person of another kind` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any of its employees, or a person under contract to it who has technical or specialized knowledge"

-- (6) The Commission must, after completing an investigation, prepare a report and provide a copy of it to the applicant and the relevant Attorney General.
-- src:19605 | Investigation report
-- src:19606 | (6) The Commission must, after completing an investigation, prepare a report and provide a copy of it to the applicant and the relevant Attorney General.
@ref s 696.5(6) (not in force) (src:19605-19606)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 696.1 (not in force) party` `s 696.1 (not in force) act`
`s 696.5(6) (not in force) the Commission must prepare a report and provide a copy of it` MEANS
    PARTY `s 696.1 (not in force) the Commission`
    MUST `s 696.5(6) (not in force) prepare a report and provide a copy of it to the applicant and the relevant Attorney General`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 696.1 (not in force) the Commission` BECAUSE "the Commission did not prepare a report after completing an investigation and provide a copy of it to the applicant and the relevant Attorney General"

@ref s 696.5(6) (not in force) (src:19605-19606)
GIVEN `the Commission has completed an investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.5(6) (not in force) the Commission owes the duty to prepare a report and provide a copy of it` MEANS
    IF `the Commission has completed an investigation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "after completing an investigation"

-- (7) The report must specify a reasonable period within which a written response may be provided to the Commission.
-- src:19607 | Deadline to respond
-- src:19608 | (7) The report must specify a reasonable period within which a written response may be provided to the Commission.
@ref s 696.5(7) (not in force) (src:19607-19608)
GIVEN `the document is the report under subsection 696.5(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.5(7) (not in force) the report must specify a reasonable period within which a written response may be provided` MEANS
    IF `the document is the report under subsection 696.5(6)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The report must specify"

-- (8) After completing the investigation, the Commission may make a decision under section 696.6 only if, within the period specified in the report, it has received either written responses or written confirmation that no responses will be provided
-- by or on behalf of the applicant and by the relevant Attorney General or if that period has ended.
-- src:19609 | Decision after investigation
-- src:19610 | (8) After completing the investigation, the Commission may make a decision under section 696.6 only if, within the period specified in the report, it has received either written responses or written confirmation that no responses will be provided by or on behalf of the applicant and by the relevant Attorney General or if that period has ended.
@ref s 696.5(8) (not in force) (src:19609-19610)
GIVEN `the investigation has been completed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `within the period specified in the report, the Commission has received either written responses or written confirmation that no responses will be provided, by or on behalf of the applicant and by the relevant Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period specified in the report has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.5(8) (not in force) the condition for deciding under section 696.6 after an investigation is met` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the investigation has been completed` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "After completing the investigation"
        IF `within the period specified in the report, the Commission has received either written responses or written confirmation that no responses will be provided, by or on behalf of the applicant and by the relevant Attorney General` OR `the period specified in the report has ended` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may make a decision under section 696.6 only if"

-- 696.6 (1) On completion of a review, the Commission must make, under this section, a decision on the application.
-- src:19611 | Decision
-- src:19612 | 696.6 (1) On completion of a review, the Commission must make, under this section, a decision on the application.
@ref s 696.6(1) (not in force) (src:19611-19612)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 696.1 (not in force) party` `s 696.1 (not in force) act`
`s 696.6(1) (not in force) the Commission must make a decision on the application` MEANS
    PARTY `s 696.1 (not in force) the Commission`
    MUST `s 696.6(1) (not in force) make a decision on the application`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 696.1 (not in force) the Commission` BECAUSE "the Commission did not make a decision on the application on completion of a review"

@ref s 696.6(1) (not in force) (src:19611-19612)
GIVEN `a review has been completed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.6(1) (not in force) the Commission owes the duty to make a decision on the application` MEANS
    IF `a review has been completed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On completion of a review"

-- (2) If the Commission has reasonable grounds to conclude that a miscarriage of justice may have occurred and considers that it is in the interests of justice to do so, it must (a) direct a new trial before any court that the Commission thinks proper or,
-- in the case of an applicant who was found to be a dangerous offender or long-term offender under Part XXIV, a new hearing under that Part; or (b) refer the matter to the court of appeal for a hearing and determination by that court as if it were an appeal by the applicant.
-- src:19613 | Remedies
-- src:19614 | (2) If the Commission has reasonable grounds to conclude that a miscarriage of justice may have occurred and considers that it is in the interests of justice to do so, it must
-- src:19615 | (a) direct a new trial before any court that the Commission thinks proper or, in the case of an applicant who was found to be a dangerous offender or long-term offender under Part XXIV, a new hearing under that Part; or
-- src:19616 | (b) refer the matter to the court of appeal for a hearing and determination by that court as if it were an appeal by the applicant.
@ref s 696.6(2) (not in force) (src:19613-19616)
GIVEN `the Commission has reasonable grounds to conclude that a miscarriage of justice may have occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission considers that it is in the interests of justice to grant a remedy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.6(2) (not in force) the Commission must grant a remedy under paragraph (a) or (b)` MEANS
    IF `the Commission has reasonable grounds to conclude that a miscarriage of justice may have occurred` AND `the Commission considers that it is in the interests of justice to grant a remedy`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Commission has reasonable grounds to conclude that a miscarriage of justice may have occurred and considers that it is in the interests of justice to do so, it must"

-- (2)(a): a new trial, or for a dangerous offender or long-term offender a new hearing under Part XXIV. Read as: for such an applicant the form is the new hearing (fork F9).
@ref s 696.6(2)(a) (not in force) (src:19615)
DECLARE `s 696.6(2)(a) (not in force) the form of the new proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `s 696.6(2)(a) (not in force) a new trial before any court that the Commission thinks proper`
    `s 696.6(2)(a) (not in force) a new hearing under Part XXIV`

@ref s 696.6(2)(a) (not in force) (src:19615)
GIVEN `the applicant was found to be a dangerous offender or long-term offender under Part XXIV` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 696.6(2)(a) (not in force) the form of the new proceeding`
`s 696.6(2)(a) (not in force) the form of the new proceeding the Commission directs` MEANS
    IF `the applicant was found to be a dangerous offender or long-term offender under Part XXIV`
    THEN `s 696.6(2)(a) (not in force) a new hearing under Part XXIV`
    ELSE `s 696.6(2)(a) (not in force) a new trial before any court that the Commission thinks proper`

-- (3) If the Commission does not grant a remedy under subsection (2), it must dismiss the application.
-- src:19617 | Dismissal of application
-- src:19618 | (3) If the Commission does not grant a remedy under subsection (2), it must dismiss the application.
@ref s 696.6(3) (not in force) (src:19617-19618)
GIVEN `the Commission does not grant a remedy under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.6(3) (not in force) the Commission must dismiss the application` MEANS
    IF `the Commission does not grant a remedy under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Commission does not grant a remedy under subsection (2), it must dismiss the application"

-- (4) If the applicant is deceased, the Commission may only refer the matter to the court of appeal under paragraph (2)(b) or dismiss the application.
-- src:19619 | Deceased applicant
-- src:19620 | (4) If the applicant is deceased, the Commission may only refer the matter to the court of appeal under paragraph (2)(b) or dismiss the application.
@ref s 696.6(4) (not in force) (src:19619-19620)
DECLARE `s 696.6(4) (not in force) the step` IS ONE OF
    `s 696.6(4) (not in force) refer the matter to the court of appeal under paragraph (2)(b)`
    `s 696.6(4) (not in force) dismiss the application`
    `s 696.6(4) (not in force) direct a new trial or a new hearing under paragraph (2)(a)`

@ref s 696.6(4) (not in force) (src:19619-19620)
GIVEN `the applicant is deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
      step IS A `s 696.6(4) (not in force) the step`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.6(4) (not in force) the Commission may take the step` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the applicant is deceased` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the applicant is deceased"
        IF step EQUALS `s 696.6(4) (not in force) direct a new trial or a new hearing under paragraph (2)(a)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Commission may only refer the matter to the court of appeal under paragraph (2)(b) or dismiss the application"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (5) In making its decision, the Commission must take into account (a) whether the application is supported by a new matter of significance that was not considered by the courts or previously considered by the Commission in an application in relation to the same finding or verdict;
-- (b) the relevance and reliability of the information; (c) the fact that an application is not intended to serve as a further appeal and that the remedies are extraordinary remedies; (d) the personal circumstances of the applicant;
-- (e) the distinct challenges that applicants who belong to certain populations face in obtaining a remedy, with particular attention to the circumstances of Indigenous or Black applicants; and (f) any other factor that it considers relevant.
-- src:19621 | Factors
-- src:19622 | (5) In making its decision, the Commission must take into account
-- src:19623 | (a) whether the application is supported by a new matter of significance that was not considered by the courts or previously considered by the Commission in an application in relation to the same finding or verdict;
-- src:19624 | (b) the relevance and reliability of the information that is presented in connection with the application;
-- src:19625 | (c) the fact that an application is not intended to serve as a further appeal and that the remedies set out in subsection (2) are extraordinary remedies;
-- src:19626 | (d) the personal circumstances of the applicant;
-- src:19627 | (e) the distinct challenges that applicants who belong to certain populations face in obtaining a remedy for a miscarriage of justice, with particular attention to the circumstances of Indigenous or Black applicants; and
-- src:19628 | (f) any other factor that it considers relevant.
@ref s 696.6(5) (not in force) (src:19621-19628)
DECLARE `s 696.6(5) (not in force) the factor` IS ONE OF
    `s 696.6(5)(a) (not in force) whether the application is supported by a new matter of significance that was not considered by the courts or previously considered by the Commission in an application in relation to the same finding or verdict`
    `s 696.6(5)(b) (not in force) the relevance and reliability of the information that is presented in connection with the application`
    `s 696.6(5)(c) (not in force) the fact that an application is not intended to serve as a further appeal and that the remedies set out in subsection (2) are extraordinary remedies`
    `s 696.6(5)(d) (not in force) the personal circumstances of the applicant`
    `s 696.6(5)(e) (not in force) the distinct challenges that applicants who belong to certain populations face in obtaining a remedy for a miscarriage of justice, with particular attention to the circumstances of Indigenous or Black applicants`
    `s 696.6(5)(f) (not in force) any other factor that it considers relevant`

@ref s 696.6(5) (not in force) (src:19621-19628)
GIVEN factor IS A `s 696.6(5) (not in force) the factor`
      `the Commission considers the factor relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.6(5) (not in force) the Commission must take the factor into account` MEANS
    CONSIDER factor
    WHEN `s 696.6(5)(a) (not in force) whether the application is supported by a new matter of significance that was not considered by the courts or previously considered by the Commission in an application in relation to the same finding or verdict` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 696.6(5)(b) (not in force) the relevance and reliability of the information that is presented in connection with the application` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 696.6(5)(c) (not in force) the fact that an application is not intended to serve as a further appeal and that the remedies set out in subsection (2) are extraordinary remedies` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 696.6(5)(d) (not in force) the personal circumstances of the applicant` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 696.6(5)(e) (not in force) the distinct challenges that applicants who belong to certain populations face in obtaining a remedy for a miscarriage of justice, with particular attention to the circumstances of Indigenous or Black applicants` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 696.6(5)(f) (not in force) any other factor that it considers relevant` THEN
        IF `the Commission considers the factor relevant`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any other factor that it considers relevant"

-- (6) For greater certainty, the Commission may grant a remedy under subsection (2) even if the evidence does not establish the innocence of the applicant.
-- src:19629 | Innocence
-- src:19630 | (6) For greater certainty, the Commission may grant a remedy under subsection (2) even if the evidence does not establish the innocence of the applicant.
@ref s 696.6(6) (not in force) (src:19629-19630)
GIVEN `the evidence does not establish the innocence of the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.6(6) (not in force) the Commission may grant a remedy under subsection (2) even if the evidence does not establish the innocence of the applicant` MEANS
    IF `the evidence does not establish the innocence of the applicant`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "even if the evidence does not establish the innocence of the applicant"

-- (7) The Commission must notify the applicant and the relevant Attorney General of its decision.
-- src:19631 | Notice
-- src:19632 | (7) The Commission must notify the applicant and the relevant Attorney General of its decision.
@ref s 696.6(7) (not in force) (src:19631-19632)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 696.1 (not in force) party` `s 696.1 (not in force) act`
`s 696.6(7) (not in force) the Commission must notify the applicant and the relevant Attorney General of its decision` MEANS
    PARTY `s 696.1 (not in force) the Commission`
    MUST `s 696.6(7) (not in force) notify the applicant and the relevant Attorney General of its decision`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 696.1 (not in force) the Commission` BECAUSE "the Commission did not notify the applicant and the relevant Attorney General of its decision"

@ref s 696.6(7) (not in force) (src:19631-19632)
GIVEN `the Commission has made its decision on the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.6(7) (not in force) the Commission owes the duty to notify the applicant and the relevant Attorney General of its decision` MEANS
    IF `the Commission has made its decision on the application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "of its decision"

§ `Court of Appeal Opinion -- section 696.61`

-- 696.61 The Commission may, at any time, refer to the court of appeal, for its opinion, any question in relation to an application on which the Commission desires the assistance of that court, and the court must provide its opinion accordingly.
-- src:19634 | Court of Appeal Opinion
-- src:19635 | Reference
-- src:19636 | 696.61 The Commission may, at any time, refer to the court of appeal, for its opinion, any question in relation to an application on which the Commission desires the assistance of that court, and the court must provide its opinion accordingly.
@ref s 696.61 (not in force) (src:19634-19636)
GIVEN `the question is in relation to an application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission desires the assistance of the court of appeal on the question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.61 (not in force) the Commission may refer the question to the court of appeal for its opinion` MEANS
    IF `the question is in relation to an application` AND `the Commission desires the assistance of the court of appeal on the question`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any question in relation to an application on which the Commission desires the assistance of that court"

@ref s 696.61 (not in force) (src:19634-19636)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 696.1 (not in force) party` `s 696.1 (not in force) act`
`s 696.61 (not in force) the court of appeal must provide its opinion` MEANS
    PARTY `s 696.61 (not in force) the court of appeal`
    MUST `s 696.61 (not in force) provide its opinion accordingly`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 696.61 (not in force) the court of appeal` BECAUSE "the court of appeal did not provide its opinion on a question the Commission referred to it"

@ref s 696.61 (not in force) (src:19634-19636)
GIVEN `the Commission has referred the question to the court of appeal for its opinion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.61 (not in force) the court of appeal must provide its opinion on the question` MEANS
    IF `the Commission has referred the question to the court of appeal for its opinion`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court must provide its opinion accordingly"

§ `2024, c. 33, ss. 5 and 6 -- section 696.7 "applicant" and section 696.72 (mandate)`

-- 5 The definition applicant in section 696.7 of the Act is replaced by: applicant has the same meaning as in section 696.1. A pointer to this module's own definition.
-- src:19643 | 5 The definition applicant in section 696.7 of the Act is replaced by the following:
-- src:19644 | applicant has the same meaning as in section 696.1. (demandeur)
@ref s 696.7 "applicant" as replaced by 2024, c. 33, s. 5 (src:19643-19644)
GIVEN `the person is the subject of the finding or verdict in question in the miscarriage of justice review application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.7 "applicant" (not in force)` MEANS `s 696.1 "applicant" (not in force)` `the person is the subject of the finding or verdict in question in the miscarriage of justice review application`

-- 6 Section 696.72 of the Act is replaced by: 696.72 The Commission's mandate is to review applications made under Part XXI.1 on the grounds of miscarriage of justice.
-- src:19647 | 6 Section 696.72 of the Act is replaced by the following:
-- src:19648 | Mandate
-- src:19649 | 696.72 The Commission’s mandate is to review applications made under Part XXI.1 on the grounds of miscarriage of justice.
@ref s 696.72 as replaced by 2024, c. 33, s. 6 (src:19647-19649)
GIVEN `the application is made under Part XXI.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is on the grounds of miscarriage of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 696.72 (not in force) the application is within the Commission’s mandate` MEANS
    IF `the application is made under Part XXI.1` AND `the application is on the grounds of miscarriage of justice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Commission’s mandate is to review applications made under Part XXI.1 on the grounds of miscarriage of justice"
